WEBVTT

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:04.150
I heard from Coach Fujitani.

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:09.220
It seems that people are saying that
I'm treating one of you with favoritism.

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:10.780
Where is that coming from?

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:16.660
Does that mean I'm giving special coaching to only one of you?

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:24.680
If you have a problem with my coaching,
please be more specific in your criticism next time.

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:31.420
Like how I tell you to raise your chin by 5mm,
or that you could've jumped half a second earlier.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.850
Well, let's begin practice then.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.120
The qualifiers for the Asian training camp are right in front of us.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:59.950
You're stumbling on the same part.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:01.700
Right.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.180
Do it again.

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:19.410
<i>Nothing is going well.</i>

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:24.980
<i>This isn't fun at all.</i>

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:16.340
Youichi...

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:21.950
I heard from Ryou and Reiji.

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:26.710
They told Coach Fujitani that
Coach Asaki was playing favorites.

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:34.130
Reiji seemed to feel bad about doing it,
but Ryou is still sulking.

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:39.430
Well, knowing him, he'll come around after a while.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:43.360
It's just the three of us.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:44.800
What do you mean?

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:48.120
We're the only three 8th grade
boys diving in Tokyo right now.

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:53.620
The only ones who know the pain of hitting the water from the 10-meter platform.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:57.130
So I always thought the two of them were special.

00:03:57.910 --> 00:04:01.630
That's why I'm shocked that the two of them turned on me like that.

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:07.010
Maybe it was that much harder for them since the three of you were special.

00:04:07.570 --> 00:04:08.210
Huh?

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:12.270
They could've started seeing you as the only different one.

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:15.270
You might be right.

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:18.930
Maybe I was getting a little carried away.

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:22.280
I do feel bad about that.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:24.790
You do?

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:26.670
You're too soft, Tomo.

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:27.780
Too soft?

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:31.700
Winning and losing is always a part of sports.

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:35.710
You interested Asaki Kayoko more than Ryou and Reiji.

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:37.850
You won.

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:41.840
It's something all athletes have accepted.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:44.870
Are you going to get depressed like this every time you win?

00:04:44.870 --> 00:04:47.050
But I still didn't know—

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:48.810
How they were feeling?

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:54.440
Neither of them ever thought
you'd all make it through together.

00:04:58.890 --> 00:05:01.860
You're not planning on quitting diving, are you?

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:02.570
Huh?

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:04.280
Listen to me, Tomo.

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:09.330
If you ever want to experience 100,000 people cheering you on in a huge arena one day,

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:11.830
then you need to forget about a couple of friends.

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:18.580
If you waste your time worrying about others,
you won't have the energy left to inspire 100,000 spectators.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:22.710
You're not going to quit, right?

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:25.280
I want to continue diving.

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:26.400
I won't quit.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:27.590
I don't want to quit.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:32.430
Then all is well.

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:35.640
Things will get boring for me if you quit.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:36.500
Huh?

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:41.400
Hey, Tomo. Do you have some time right now?

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:42.900
I do.

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:45.170
Okay, I'll treat you to dinner then.

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:53.830
One iced coffee.

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:55.490
That's it?

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:57.160
You're not going to eat a burger?

00:05:57.630 --> 00:05:58.810
Of course not.

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:01.780
I'd never eat anything this high in calories.

00:06:02.490 --> 00:06:04.880
Wait, were you going to have a burger?

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:06.190
No.

00:06:06.190 --> 00:06:07.630
An iced tea, please.

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:10.180
You need to count your calories!

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:14.430
How could you even think about eating something this high in calories?

00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:16.210
Huh?

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:29.240
Take a look at this.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:31.330
Competitive Swimming Monthly

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:33.710
"The Death of a Diving Master"?

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:37.450
"August 29th, 2010.

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:44.230
While fishing in the waters of Aomori, a small fishing boat was capsized by a wave during Typhoon No. 19.

00:06:44.230 --> 00:06:48.970
Mr. Okitsu Shiraha and his oldest son Hiromi were both on board the boat and drowned.

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:49.010
Competitive Swimming Monthly

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:53.610
Seeing that small article in the newspaper last month,

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:58.510
surely I was not the only one to have memories of yesteryears come suddenly flooding back.

00:06:58.510 --> 00:07:03.630
Okitsu Shiraha is a name that once heard cannot be easily forgotten."

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:05.400
Is this...

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:08.420
Yeah, it's about Okitsu's grandfather.

00:07:10.090 --> 00:07:15.240
"If Okitsu only had the right environment in which to thrive during his peak.

00:07:16.090 --> 00:07:22.230
Aging as his talents went unrealized,
the pain of a prodigy returning home uncrowned.

00:07:22.230 --> 00:07:23.750
It pains me to this day.

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:32.060
For the soul of a master diver sleeping in Tsugaru's ocean,
our condolences may not be enough for him to rest in peace."

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:37.520
Wow, how did you find this?

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:41.100
You know how my mom helps out with the Japan Swimming Federation?

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:43.960
Any news like this gets saved.

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:46.270
So, what do you think about the article?

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:48.150
What do you mean?

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:52.780
So I guess Okitsu's father and grandfather both passed away at sea.

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:55.780
Do you feel a grudge?

00:07:56.070 --> 00:07:57.320
Grudge?

00:07:57.320 --> 00:07:58.250
Whose?

00:07:58.250 --> 00:08:01.240
Okitsu Shiraha's of course.

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:02.450
Why?

00:08:02.450 --> 00:08:03.600
What do you mean, "why"?

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:07.100
According to this article, Okitsu Shiraha had talent,

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:11.550
but his career ended before he had the time to hone his skills or the stage to showcase them.

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:13.210
What would you do if that were you?

00:08:13.850 --> 00:08:16.550
Well, I'd be pretty frustrated.

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:17.770
Right?

00:08:17.770 --> 00:08:22.490
I feel Shiraha's anger when I watch Okitsu's diving.

00:08:22.490 --> 00:08:27.310
He had the talent, but he sacrificed everything for diving.

00:08:28.180 --> 00:08:31.640
He had to endure so many things while dedicating his whole life to diving,

00:08:31.640 --> 00:08:37.070
but in the end diving didn't give anything back to Okitsu Shiraha.

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:40.440
If anything, it took everything away from him.

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:41.610
Well, that's...

00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:51.270
I mean, you're right. Sometimes I feel like maybe I would've been happier if I never started diving.

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:56.240
I hear you're having trouble getting to the three-and-a-half.

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:57.340
Yeah.

00:08:57.810 --> 00:08:59.400
Don't give up.

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:00.940
There's something you need to remember.

00:09:01.590 --> 00:09:05.610
Asaki Kayoko isn't the only one who believes in you.

00:09:05.610 --> 00:09:06.360
What?

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:08.230
I'm talking about me.

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:12.320
Whenever I watch you dive,
there's something that sticks out to me.

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:13.360
I've always felt it.

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:15.990
That's why I have my eye on you.

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:17.240
Eye on me?

00:09:17.650 --> 00:09:19.180
Watch your back.

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:24.440
Maybe the reason I'm looking after you like this is so I can trip you up one day.

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:44.910
Tomo, did Youichi talk to you?

00:09:44.910 --> 00:09:45.770
Yeah.

00:09:46.510 --> 00:09:50.040
We were just feeling really angry with you lately.

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:51.150
That's why...

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:52.650
I feel bad—

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:53.650
You're soft.

00:09:58.340 --> 00:09:59.880
We're sorry.

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:01.190
Right, Ryou?

00:10:01.190 --> 00:10:02.160
Yeah.

00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:07.800
We were jealous of you.

00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:10.380
Something we were made acutely aware of.

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:12.000
I understand your point.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:17.680
You two also want a clearer goal and more specific instructions.

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:19.430
Okay.

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:24.130
I'll point out something specific to you right now.

00:10:24.130 --> 00:10:28.760
You two don't do the individual training I assigned you every day, do you?

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:33.280
Before you envy others,
you need to be doing everything you should.

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:37.560
She really let us have it.

00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:39.710
It hurt because she was right.

00:10:39.710 --> 00:10:43.510
So we both decided to first do what we should be doing.

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:51.090
I'm not going to lose to you. Got it?

00:10:54.980 --> 00:10:55.670
Right.

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:03.970
Ready? Go!

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:07.730
Try to get the timing down!

00:11:08.010 --> 00:11:09.380
Ready to go again.

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:23.240
There isn't any time before the qualifiers.

00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:25.240
You need to shape up!

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:27.380
Man, he's stubborn.

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:32.380
I don't need saving.

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:34.250
That's what the old man said.

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:38.280
Saving is one of the most important techniques a diver can have.

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:42.380
Entering the water perpendicularly
allows you to enter without a splash.

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:46.390
But there's no way to get the angle to be exactly 90 degrees.

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:49.070
It's either too steep or too shallow of an angle.

00:11:49.070 --> 00:11:52.390
Saving is controlling that deviation.

00:11:53.410 --> 00:11:55.520
I don't need it.

00:11:55.520 --> 00:12:01.400
The old man was trying to teach me how to enter
the water completely straight without cheap tricks.

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:04.400
That was the old way of thinking.

00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:06.850
It's something that's essential now.

00:12:06.850 --> 00:12:09.360
Diving is an aerial competition.

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:12.410
Since when did it become a competition about counting splashes?

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:16.280
Since the 1964 Tokyo Olympics.

00:12:16.280 --> 00:12:19.550
The same one your grandfather Okitsu Shiraha aimed for.

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:25.430
An American diver performed a
perfect rip entry to great fanfare.

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:28.930
The technique spread rapidly after that.

00:12:29.630 --> 00:12:33.260
And so they became timid, too scared of making a splash.

00:12:33.260 --> 00:12:34.450
Ridiculous.

00:12:39.260 --> 00:12:41.900
Do you feel a grudge?

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:43.210
Grudge?

00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:44.140
Whose?

00:12:44.140 --> 00:12:46.950
Okitsu Shiraha's of course.

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:49.450
Maybe it's true.

00:12:52.690 --> 00:12:53.970
Asaki.

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:54.960
Yes?

00:12:55.300 --> 00:12:57.970
You shouldn't be too fixated on results.

00:12:58.250 --> 00:12:58.830
What?

00:12:59.580 --> 00:13:02.810
Diving is a sport that demands a great amount of time.

00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:08.000
Their futures are still far off into the distance, and their road is a long one.

00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:14.980
I do understand that you're thinking about
shortcuts in order to save MDC from closure.

00:13:15.670 --> 00:13:18.990
But our role as coaches is not about shortcuts,

00:13:19.370 --> 00:13:21.940
but to teach them about the long road ahead.

00:13:23.430 --> 00:13:24.360
I...

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:28.950
Sorry, maybe it wasn't my place to say anything.

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:30.370
Forget about it.

00:13:44.680 --> 00:13:47.500
Use your eyes.

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:50.590
It's all about the first one.

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:56.640
Even if you only pull this move off once, you'll get the hang of it right away.

00:13:57.160 --> 00:13:59.650
Memorize the feel of a three-and-a-half after just one time.

00:14:00.510 --> 00:14:02.150
I know you can do that.

00:14:02.490 --> 00:14:04.950
As long as you manage to overcome the initial hurdle.

00:14:09.040 --> 00:14:10.910
What did Coach Asaki say?

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:13.660
It'll be easy if I can just do it once.

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:17.450
The problem is that you're having trouble getting that first one under your belt.

00:14:18.720 --> 00:14:20.920
I don't feel like I can do it.

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:26.170
But I have to.

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:29.930
Okay, I'm off.

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:32.550
I hope you'll be able to see the stars.

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:34.020
Don't worry.

00:14:34.020 --> 00:14:37.500
All us stargazers have good luck when it comes to weather.

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:41.500
More importantly, Tomoki,
are you really going to be okay on your own?

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:44.570
Maybe you should've gone camping with Hiroya.

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:48.070
I've got practice, and I don't know Hiroya's friends very well.

00:14:48.490 --> 00:14:50.170
Then you could come with us...

00:14:50.170 --> 00:14:52.080
I'll be fine!

00:15:04.180 --> 00:15:06.340
Sorry to keep you waiting, Chikuwa! Ready to go home?

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:19.880
Okitsu?!

00:15:19.880 --> 00:15:20.600
Huh?

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:22.140
What are you doing here?

00:15:22.140 --> 00:15:23.440
Killing time.

00:15:29.350 --> 00:15:30.610
Thanks.

00:15:32.840 --> 00:15:34.340
My roommate...

00:15:34.340 --> 00:15:35.620
Coach Ooshima?

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:38.060
He talks a lot.

00:15:38.060 --> 00:15:41.870
Sometimes I want to be alone, so I come here when I do.

00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:45.550
What is it?

00:15:45.550 --> 00:15:50.070
Sorry, it's just that I've never talked to you like this before.

00:15:50.070 --> 00:15:52.890
We've never really talked during practice.

00:15:52.890 --> 00:15:54.810
It's by habit.

00:15:54.810 --> 00:15:57.460
It's mostly just been me and my gramps.

00:15:57.460 --> 00:15:59.890
I don't got a lot of experience hanging out with friends.

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:02.680
And I'm also not a fan of pools.

00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:05.400
I feel suffocated when I'm there.

00:16:05.740 --> 00:16:07.400
You hate the pool?

00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:09.460
Yeah, it's cramped.

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:15.660
And thinking about how many points the stupid judges are gonna give me for my dive doesn't really jive with me.

00:16:16.210 --> 00:16:19.540
Then what's diving to you?

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:25.220
It's not about grudges or revenge, is it?

00:16:25.220 --> 00:16:28.270
You don't hate diving, do you?

00:16:28.270 --> 00:16:30.570
No way. Of course not.

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:35.680
If I had to say it's anything, maybe it's the Okitsu blood.

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:38.180
Okitsu blood?

00:16:38.180 --> 00:16:41.930
Yeah, the Okitsu family has been the
leader of the fishermen for generations,

00:16:42.220 --> 00:16:47.640
and they'd jump from a cliff when the catch was poor in a ritual to appease the god of the sea.

00:16:47.640 --> 00:16:53.480
Although, they stopped the practice during my dad's time,
saying it was too dangerous and outdated.

00:16:53.480 --> 00:16:56.450
But my gramps continued to teach me how to dive.

00:16:57.160 --> 00:16:59.200
I don't believe in a god of the sea,

00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:02.470
but the Okitsu blood believes in one.

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:06.460
This blood compels me to challenge the ocean.

00:17:06.760 --> 00:17:08.790
That's my diving.

00:17:09.850 --> 00:17:13.220
So why am I stuck doing it in a pool?

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:19.660
But I think your grandfather might've wanted you to become a diver who was effective in the pool too.

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:20.850
No way!

00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:23.440
Gramps hated pools too.

00:17:23.440 --> 00:17:27.350
While he was an athlete, pools were basically a nightmare.

00:17:27.910 --> 00:17:32.380
Then how are you able to do a forward one-and-a-half pike?

00:17:32.380 --> 00:17:33.480
What?

00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:39.870
And the other moves you can do are all standard moves divers use for meets.

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:43.000
Your body alignment was already perfect too.

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:46.980
So are you saying my gramps wanted my dives to be scored,

00:17:46.980 --> 00:17:50.000
or that he wanted me to enter the water gently to please some judges?!

00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:54.050
Sorry, that I don't know.

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:57.130
But I don't really care about judges either.

00:17:59.290 --> 00:18:02.130
I always want to overcome something.

00:18:02.130 --> 00:18:03.640
I want to break out.

00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:07.140
And that's why I dive.

00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:10.430
It's not about winning some competition.

00:18:10.430 --> 00:18:14.780
I'm just waiting for my moment to shine.

00:18:15.430 --> 00:18:17.450
A view only I can see.

00:18:18.090 --> 00:18:20.280
Those are the type of things I'm diving for.

00:18:21.040 --> 00:18:24.820
Your moment to shine that only belongs to you, huh?

00:18:27.030 --> 00:18:31.420
I've got a feeling you'll be able to make that three-and-a-half.

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:35.170
Later.

00:19:09.720 --> 00:19:10.460
You did it!

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:16.210
Wow.

00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:19.720
You did it, Tomo!

00:19:22.660 --> 00:19:25.960
<i>I have to do it again before I forget what this feels like.</i>

00:19:26.780 --> 00:19:29.750
<i>A three-and-a-half. One more rotation than usual.</i>

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:32.300
<i>Another lap around the world.</i>

00:19:34.660 --> 00:19:37.900
The wind is starting to pick up, so let's call it a day.

00:19:52.140 --> 00:19:53.230
I'm home.

00:20:02.420 --> 00:20:04.140
You here, Hiro?

00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:08.290
Hey, Hiro. Answer me if you're here.

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:11.140
You're back early, Tomo.

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:13.400
Practice let out early because of the weather.

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:16.900
Anyway, I finally did a three-and-a-half!

00:20:17.600 --> 00:20:18.800
Really? That's great.

00:20:20.950 --> 00:20:23.030
What's going on? Is someone here?

00:20:23.030 --> 00:20:23.910
Huh?

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:25.520
It's nothing.

00:20:25.520 --> 00:20:26.410
Don't worry about it.

00:20:26.930 --> 00:20:29.410
Did you bring a girlfriend here or something?

00:20:30.920 --> 00:20:32.700
Wait, seriously?

00:20:33.170 --> 00:20:35.670
Then stop hiding her and introduce me already!

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:38.170
Stop!

00:21:04.020 --> 00:21:11.750
<i>In that instant, I felt like I was dropped somewhere much darker and deeper than a diving pool.</i>

00:21:12.730 --> 00:21:14.280
<i>There was nothing there.</i>

00:21:14.950 --> 00:21:17.110
<i>No color, no smells.</i>

00:21:17.910 --> 00:21:19.030
<i>Not even a sound.</i>
